#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Sets Omarchy-Buddy up after `omarchy plugin add` (or again after an
# update; it only changes what is not set yet), and with --remove takes it
# all back out.
#
#   omarchy-buddy-setup               set up; in a terminal it first lists the
#                                     files it changes and asks once (#208;
#                                     No: nothing changes, exit 1)
#   omarchy-buddy-setup --yes         set up without asking (install.sh)
#   omarchy-buddy-setup --remove      Omarchy's notifications back, hooks out
#   omarchy-buddy-setup --uninstall   --remove, then `omarchy plugin remove`
#                                     (the button in the island's settings)
#   omarchy-buddy-setup --commands on|off   only the line for long terminal
#                                     commands (the island's switch; exit 2:
#                                     chezmoi has the file, add it there)
#   omarchy-buddy-setup --agents      the agents that are installed (their
#                                     folder is there, Claude's too), for the island
#   omarchy-buddy-setup --agent NAME on|off   one agent's hooks or plugin in
#                                     or out (the island's switch; it writes
#                                     agents.NAME to config.json; exit 2: a
#                                     file of the agent's stayed as it was)
#   omarchy-buddy-setup --weather on|off   Omarchy's weather out of the bar
#                                     or back where it stood (the island's
#                                     switch, it writes config.json "weather")
#   omarchy-buddy-setup --bar [on|off]   "Leiste ordnen": the clock, O-Morchy,
#                                     Omarchy's indicators side by side, or
#                                     back; prints offer, undo or nothing
#   … --files-only                    only files: no systemctl, no shell
#                                     restart (tests in a sandbox HOME)
#
# Setting up:
#   - the scripts in ~/.local/bin and the Omarchy post-update and battery-low hooks
#   - ~/.claude/settings.json: the hook for every event and
#     omarchy-buddy-statusline in front of the status line (the old one is
#     kept in ~/.local/state/omarchy-buddy/statusline.json and keeps running).
#     Both commands do nothing (the status line: run the old one) once the
#     script is gone, e.g. after `omarchy plugin remove` without --remove.
#   - ~/.codex/hooks.json: the hook (with --codex) for Codex's events, and
#     in ~/.codex/config.toml the hashes that say the user trusts them
#     ([hooks.state."…"], also for Omarchy 4.5's further Codex accounts,
#     which share both files), so Codex does not ask about them at start.
#   - the hook (with --agent NAME) for Gemini CLI (~/.gemini/settings.json),
#     Crush (~/.config/crush/crush.json) and GitHub Copilot CLI (its own
#     ~/.copilot/hooks/omarchy-buddy.json), and Omarchy 4.5's Antigravity
#     (~/.gemini/config/hooks.json), Qwen Code, Kimi, Devin, Command Code and
#     Kiro, each only where its folder is, see AGENT_HOOKS. Grok and Cursor
#     run the Claude hooks above as they are.
#   - opencode, Pi and Oh My Pi: our plugin file in their plugin folder
#     (~/.config/opencode/plugins, ~/.pi/agent/extensions,
#     ~/.omp/agent/extensions), see AGENT_PLUGINS
#   - an agent off in config.json ("agents": {"NAME": false}) gets none
#     of the above, what is there of ours comes out; Claude is always on
#   - ~/.config/omarchy/shell.json: Omarchy's own notifications plugin off
#     (there can be only one notification server), its Dnd indicator out of
#     the bar (the island has the Ruhemodus), this plugin on: its bar widget
#     right after Omarchy's clock (#182; where the user moved it, it stays);
#     with "weather" on in config.json Omarchy's weather out of the bar (#184)
#   - the systemd user timer for omarchy-buddy-feed
#   - while "longCommands" is on in config.json: a marked line in ~/.bashrc
#     and ~/.zshrc that loads lib/long-commands.sh (not in a file chezmoi
#     manages: the setup names the line instead)
# Every file is backed up before it changes (*.bak-omarchy-buddy-TIME, the
# newest 3 per file stay); what shell.json looked like is kept in setup.json,
# so --remove puts back exactly that and leaves everything else the user
# changed since.

